      "math_academy_id": "q-37028",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $h$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $4$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $h(x)$ | $6$ | $6$ | $6$ | $0$ | $6$ | $0$ | $6$ | $0$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $h(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $h(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{0,6\\}.$",
